From b16db020b6b54aab507712e4cee85be385dd9909 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: The browser Authors <noreply@browser.invalid>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 03:23:59 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 16/61] recording

Browser.startRecording, stopRecording, recordingMask, recordingStatus and
the recordingEnded event: a network-service TrafficRecorder that sees every
load and websocket of every process and writes a HAR with bodies and
socket frames, masking the values the caller names; at level full each
renderer also reports every compiled script through V8's new
CompiledScriptCallback (see the v8 patch) and blink's ScriptRecorder.
The Browser-domain registration rides in agent-fetch (browser_handler.*,
Browser.pdl); the renderer switch forwarding rides in switch-resolver,
while the script-recording hooks in render_process_host_impl.cc are this
commit's own. Response headers reach the recording as their own list (a
response head loses its cookie lines on the way to the browser process),
so Set-Cookie is kept, on redirect hops too, and the HAR's request and
response cookies lists are filled from Cookie and Set-Cookie after
masking. Its renderer.mojom, render_thread_impl.*, blink.h and
blink_initializer.cc also carry video-recording's SetAgentRedaction
beside their SetScriptRecording twins: the browser arms every renderer
for a redacted video recording through them.
